{"pageid":3363,"title":"Corrupt Biome","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Corrupt Biome</span>","revid":18627,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/f/fb/Corrupt_cave.png/revision/latest?cb=20241011021032\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"A hole in a mountain located in the corrupt biome.\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/f/fb/Corrupt_cave.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241011021032\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"88\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Corrupt cave.png\" data-image-key=\"Corrupt_cave.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Corrupt_cave.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">A hole in a mountain located in the corrupt biome.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure><p>The <b>Corrupt biome</b> was an area located in The Desert. It was added during the 2024 Halloween event with purplish red and purple ground with purple crystals, and WAS mistaken to be a permanent addition. However, only the materials were stated to be permanent.\n</p><p>This biome was possibly a reference to the The Corruption from Terraria.\n</p><p>In this area you could find: <a href=\"/wiki/Corrupt_Deadwood\" title=\"Corrupt Deadwood\">Corrupt Deadwood</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Corrupted_Cactus\" title=\"Corrupted Cactus\">Corrupted Cactus</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Corrupt_Acacia\" title=\"Corrupt Acacia\">Corrupt Acacia</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Corrupted_limestone\" title=\"Corrupted limestone\">Corrupted Limestone</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Corrupted_tumbleweed\" title=\"Corrupted tumbleweed\">corrupted tumbleweed</a>.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/4/4b/Screenshot_2024-11-03_103930.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20241103024028\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Corruption hole from afar.\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/4/4b/Screenshot_2024-11-03_103930.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241103024028\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"91\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Screenshot 2024-11-03 103930.jpg\" data-image-key=\"Screenshot_2024-11-03_103930.jpg\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Screenshot_2024-11-03_103930.jpg\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">Corruption hole from afar.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/3/34/Corruption.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20241103024514\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"This was the supposed corruption core causing the Corruption around the Oke Desert\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/3/34/Corruption.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241103024514\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"128\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Corruption.jpg\" data-image-key=\"Corruption.jpg\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Corruption.jpg\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">This was the supposed corruption core causing the Corruption around the Oke Desert</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<p>The supposed source of corruption was a large <a href=\"/wiki/Infused_Core\" title=\"Infused Core\">infused core</a> with floating boulders surrounding it.\n</p><p>During the Halloween updates, the corruption seemed to grow larger per update.\n</p><p>It seems the corruption is related to <a href=\"/wiki/Mysterious_Mushrooms\" title=\"Mysterious Mushrooms\">mysterious mushrooms</a> and that it causes the corruption like the mysterious mushrooms itself gained a purpose to \"invade and conquer\" causing the large <a href=\"/wiki/Infused_Core\" title=\"Infused Core\">infused core</a> or the supposed corruption core to be created. \n</p><p>Evidence suggests that the corrupted meteor caused the caves and surrounding biomes to begin corrupting, yet somehow the corruption receded to only be in the caves. The only remaining remnant of the once growing spread of corruption are the Mysterious Mushrooms (and crystals) which cause any material hit with one of it's spores to turn into its subsequent corrupted variant.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/c/c7/Corrupt_core.png/revision/latest?cb=20241116184554\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"The corrupt core is nowhere to be seen leaving a huge hole behind\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"113\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Corrupt core.png\" data-image-key=\"Corrupt_core.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/c/c7/Corrupt_core.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241116184554\" /></a> \t<noscript><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/c/c7/Corrupt_core.png/revision/latest?cb=20241116184554\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"The corrupt core is nowhere to be seen leaving a huge hole behind\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/c/c7/Corrupt_core.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241116184554\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"113\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Corrupt core.png\" data-image-key=\"Corrupt_core.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/c/c7/Corrupt_core.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241116184554\" /></a></noscript> \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Corrupt_core.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">The tunnel after the biome was removed.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<p>The corrupted meteor used to reside in a tunnel it created, leading to a small underground area. However, as of now, the meteor has been removed and only the tunnel remains.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903134610\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 1/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:3363-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260903134610 and revision id 18627. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>","categories":[],"links":[{"title":"Corrupt Acacia","exists":true},{"title":"Corrupt Deadwood","exists":true},{"title":"Corrupted Cactus","exists":true},{"title":"Corrupted limestone","exists":true},{"title":"Corrupted tumbleweed","exists":true},{"title":"Infused Core","exists":true